"https://lobste.rs/s/nkmtqk/understanding_you_are_not_expected"},{"short_id":"obzyyl","created_at":"2026-11-26T04:07:43.445-06:00","title":"Confiscating the Commons, part 1: The invention of proprietary software","url":"https://ploum.net/2026-11-23-invention_proprietary_software.html","score":4,"flags":0,"comment_count":2,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"pieq","user_is_author":false,"tags":["culture","education","historical","linux"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/obzyyl","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/obzyyl/confiscating_commons_part_1_invention"},{"short_id":"3lkriu","created_at":"2026-11-26T03:45:42.146-06:00","title":"Ansible Fails waiting for privilege escalation on Ubuntu 26","url":"https://www.jeffgeerling.com/blog/2026/ansible-fails-become-ubuntu2604/","score":11,"flags":0,"comment_count":13,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"ema-pe","user_is_author":false,"tags":["devops","linux"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/3lkriu","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/3lkriu/ansible_fails_waiting_for_privilege"},{"short_id":"2kwjb4","created_at":"2026-11-26T02:02:18.480-06:00","title":"Qualcomm’s Oryon 3 Reaches the Top","url":"https://chipsandcheese.com/p/qualcomms-oryon-3-reaches-the-top","score":10,"flags":0,"comment_count":4,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"fanf","user_is_author":false,"tags":["hardware"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/2kwjb4","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/2kwjb4/qualcomm_s_oryon_3_reaches_top"},{"short_id":"w4kxiz","created_at":"2026-11-26T00:39:00.543-06:00","title":"How WinHelp files work","url":"https://quin.fyi/posts/how-winhelp-files-work.html","score":18,"flags":0,"comment_count":8,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"Quin","user_is_author":true,"tags":["programming","reversing","rust","show"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/w4kxiz","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/w4kxiz/how_winhelp_files_work"},{"short_id":"bl8gp8","created_at":"2026-11-26T00:35:12.183-06:00","title":"Meaningful Human-in-the-Loop Checking of  GenAI Synthesis for Restricted Languages","url":"https://www.siddharthaprasad.com/papers/pafk-pick.pdf","score":1,"flags":2,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eAbstract: Developers routinely use GenAI tools (large language models enriched in various ways) to generate useful components of programs, such as regular expressions. While pleasant and often effective, this can easily lead to subtle bugs. The developer may have been unclear in their specification, they may not fully understand the language of the output, there may be systematic misconceptions suffered by the user and perhaps even embedded in the language model, and so on.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResponsible use of GenAI requires humans in the loop. To be effective, the human interaction must be both meaningful and moderate. We accomplish this as follows. First, we generate multiple candidate expressions instead of one. We then use formal language containment properties to generate distinguishing concrete scenarios that illustrate the differences between the candidates. We then have users rate these concrete scenarios. This process converges in a few steps, while also giving the user insight into any lack of clarity on their part.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe have built a tool, PICK, that implements this iterative process. We apply it to three formal languages with the necessary properties: regexes, linear temporal logic, and access-control policies. We show through experiments that PICK is a significant improvement over showing users the candidate expressions, and also helps catch situations where no output is a match.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Abstract: Developers routinely use GenAI tools (large language models enriched in various ways) to generate useful components of programs, such as regular expressions. While pleasant and often effective, this can easily lead to subtle bugs. The developer may have been unclear in their specification, they may not fully understand the language of the output, there may be systematic misconceptions suffered by the user and perhaps even embedded in the language model, and so on.\r\n\r\nResponsible use of GenAI requires humans in the loop. To be effective, the human interaction must be both meaningful and moderate. We accomplish this as follows. First, we generate multiple candidate expressions instead of one. We then use formal language containment properties to generate distinguishing concrete scenarios that illustrate the differences between the candidates. We then have users rate these concrete scenarios. This process converges in a few steps, while also giving the user insight into any lack of clarity on their part.\r\n\r\nWe have built a tool, PICK, that implements this iterative process. We apply it to three formal languages with the necessary properties: regexes, linear temporal logic, and access-control policies. We show through experiments that PICK is a significant improvement over showing users the candidate expressions, and also helps catch situations where no output is a match.","submitter_user":"typesanitizer","user_is_author":false,"tags":["building-ai-tooling","pdf"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bl8gp8","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/bl8gp8/meaningful_human_loop_checking_genai"},{"short_id":"hge0sd","created_at":"2026-11-25T22:57:04.708-06:00","title":"Browser tabs as a container runtime","url":"https://fzakaria.com/2026/11/25/browser-tabs-as-a-container-runtime","score":22,"flags":1,"comment_count":4,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"mrw","user_is_author":false,"tags":["browsers"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/hge0sd","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/hge0sd/browser_tabs_as_container_runtime"},{"short_id":"2thnmt","created_at":"2026-11-25T21:56:07.099-06:00","title":"I Booted From My Tape Backup From 2002","url":"https://changelog.complete.org/archives